# Accepted findings of `trivy config`. Every entry needs a justification.

# GCP-0072: allow-internal opens every port, but only to the VPC's own node, Pod and
# Service ranges. Pods talk to each other on arbitrary ports across nodes; in-cluster
# segmentation is enforced by NetworkPolicy (Dataplane V2), not by VPC firewall rules.
GCP-0072

# KSV-0125: the sample application pulls podinfo from Docker Hub on purpose so it runs
# anywhere. Real workloads should pull from your own Artifact Registry.
KSV-0125
